    "summary": "The chat shell embeds the pager: it is created before the registry and handed it; line(), renderDiff and the approval card append through pager.append, so nothing else writes the transcript's scroll position; session-restored resets the pager and replays rows keyed and stamped by absolute index; transcript-page goes to prepend; live rows and the user row are tracked with their row index; the 'load earlier' bar sits above the transcript; the provider lock settles from total. The three shell-text pins are updated in this task. Beyond the plan's text pins, a new chat-shell.test.ts runs the real inline script against the shared fake DOM and drives it with host messages (windowed restore, page request, a live row while scrolled up, trimming a long active session). The host still sends the whole transcript.",
